    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d42">

                <pb facs="0112" n="52" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg52"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gresham to Mr.
                            Thompson</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-01-07"><hi rendition="#italic">January 7,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 204.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your No. 316, of November
                    21 last, reporting the ceremonies attending the laying of the corner stone of a
                    monument to be erected in memory of President Monroe at Rio de Janeiro.</p>
                <p>This tribute to the memory of an American statesman can not fail to be
                    appreciated by the Government and people of the United States.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. Q. Gresham</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
